@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Option Desk - Historical backtest from prices to uncertainty

start
:Load permitted history and settings;
:Validate history length;
while (Entry plus holding period fits history?) is (yes)
 :Estimate volatility from trailing returns;
 if (Volatility is usable?) then (yes)
  :Build model-priced option chain;
  :Call structure builder;
  if (A viable plan exists?) then (yes)
   :Record entry legs and capital at risk;
   :Settle payoff at historical exit spot;
   :Record return on risk when defined;
  else (no)
   :Record skipped entry and reason;
  endif
 else (no)
  :Record skipped entry and reason;
 endif
 :Advance by entry spacing;
endwhile (no)
:Summarize returns and drawdown in risk units;
:Block sign-flip randomization and moving-block bootstrap;
:Include buy-and-hold benchmark and model limitations;
:Validate and save backtest artifact;
stop
note right
The pricing tenor uses trading days / 252.
Historical option quotes and execution are not replayed.
Two-expiry builders need inputs this runner does not supply.
Sign flips require a symmetry assumption.
Block boundaries lose some dependence.
One available bootstrap block gives no interval variation.
end note

caption Sources: engine backtest/runner.py and stats.py; shell cli/backtest.py.
@enduml
